{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.he4_body_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.he4_body_order","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactSimplex.lean#L200-L205","doc":"The `A ≤ 4` half is pure counting: the complete graph on `A` vertices has\n`C(A,2)` edges, and the body-order weights of `⁴He` are the binomials\n`C(4,2), C(4,3), C(4,4) = 6, 4, 1` — the `6 a_D² + 4 a_D³ + 1 a_D⁴` of the\nfrontier note. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.no_complete_contact_of_five_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.no_complete_contact_of_five_le","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactSimplex.lean#L156-L167","doc":"**No `A ≥ 5` equal spheres are all mutually tangent** — the general form of\n\"A≥5 saturates below\". Restricting to any five reduces it to\n`not_five_equidistant`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.not_five_equidistant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.not_five_equidistant","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactSimplex.lean#L143-L154","doc":"**No five equal spheres are mutually tangent in three dimensions.**\n\nThis is the `A ≥ 5` half of \"A≤4 simplex = C(A,2), A≥5 saturates below\": the\ncontact graph of five equal spheres cannot be complete, so its bond count is\nstrictly below `C(5,2) = 10`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.card_le_finrank_succ_of_equidistant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.card_le_finrank_succ_of_equidistant","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactSimplex.lean#L135-L141","doc":"**At most `finrank + 1` points can be pairwise equidistant.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.linearIndependent_spokes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.linearIndependent_spokes","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactSimplex.lean#L79-L133","doc":"**The spokes are linearly independent.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.inner_spokes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MaxContactSimplex.inner_spokes","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MaxContactSimplex.lean#L57-L77","doc":"**The Gram entry.** For a pairwise-equidistant family based at `p 0`, any two\ndistinct spokes meet at inner product `c²/2`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}